al hash recomputation is claimed. The effective evidence set is S1 only. The original PDF governs; extracted text is the active reading representation, not independent corroboration. Source tools read the original PDF's text directly. No external URLs or incorporated documents were opened or followed.\\n\\nThe document identifies itself as **FORM 10-K**, \\u201cTransDigm Group Incorporated,\\u201d and \\u201cFor the fiscal year ended September 30, 2024\\u201d ([S1 PDF p.1](S1-annual-report.pdf#page=1)). This establishes identity from content, not filename. It is a signed annual report rather than a draft: the signature page states it was signed \\u201con November 7, 2024\\u201d and displays `/s/` signatures ([p.100](S1-annual-report.pdf#page=100)). The auditor's report is signed `/s/ Ernst & Young LLP` and dated November 7, 2024 ([p.104](S1-annual-report.pdf#page=104)). No competing version or amendment is supplied. The SEC filing/accession date is not independently verified; do not infer it from the filename.\\n\\nThe auditor's source opinion says the statements \\u201cpresent fairly, in all material respects\\u201d and are \\u201cin conformity with U.S. generally accepted accounting principles\\u201d ([p.103](S1-annual-report.pdf#page=103)). This is attribution of the document's audit opinion, not independent assurance by CP-0 or certification of extraction fidelity. Exhibit indexes and proxy references are not the underlying executed instruments or proxy itself.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n### Identity, perimeter, dates and conventions\\n\\n- **Consolidation:** Note 1 says the statements \\u201cinclude the accounts of TD Group and subsidiaries\\u201d and \\u201cIntercompany balances and transactions have been eliminated\\u201d ([S1 PDF p.110](S1-annual-report.pdf#page=110)). Page 3 defines the Company as TD Group together with TransDigm Inc. and its wholly-owned and majority-owned subsidiaries with a controlling interest. These are consolidated group statements, not TransDigm Inc. standalone, a restricted-group covenant perimeter, or guarantor-only accounts. Noncontrolling interests are separately presented on the primary statements.\\n- **Accounting basis:** Note 1 states \\u201cprepared in conformity with U.S. GAAP\\u201d and notes prior-year reclassifications to current presentation, \\u201cnone of which are material\\u201d (p.110). Preserve the report's comparative presentation; CP-0 has not reconstructed original prior-year filings.\\n- **Period policy:** \\u201cReferences to \\u2018fiscal year\\u2019 mean the year ending or ended September 30\\u201d; FY2024 is \\u201cthe period from October 1, 2023 to September 30, 2024\\u201d ([p.3](S1-annual-report.pdf#page=3)). Balance sheets are instants at September 30, 2024 and 2023 (p.105). Income, comprehensive income, equity movements and cash flows cover fiscal years ended September 30, 2024, 2023 and 2022 (pp.106\\u2013109). The equity statement also carries the opening September 30, 2021 balance; that is not an extra annual income-statement column.\\n- **Money versus shares:** Balance sheet and equity statement headers say \\u201cAmounts in millions, except share amounts\\u201d (pp.105,108); income says \\u201cAmounts in millions, except per share amounts\\u201d (p.106); comprehensive income and cash flows say \\u201cAmounts in millions\\u201d (pp.107,109). Monetary reporting is U.S. dollars: Note 1 explicitly describes translation into \\u201cU.S. dollars\\u201d (p.114), and statements carry dollar signs. Thus preserve USD millions for money, actual share counts where excepted, millions of weighted-average shares on the income statement, and USD per share for EPS and dividends. Note 4 labels its EPS computation \\u201cin millions, except per share data\\u201d (p.122). Do not apply one blanket multiplier to a whole statement.\\n- **EPS and attribution:** Note 1 specifies the \\u201ctwo-class method\\u201d (p.114); Note 4 separates common shares and vested options deemed participating securities (p.122). Preserve distinctions between consolidated net income, TD Group-attributable income and income applicable to common stockholders; do not silently substitute one for another.\\n- **As-of separation:** The report and audit signatures postdate September 30, 2024. Page 131 explicitly labels an October 2024 securitization draw \\u201cSubsequent Event\\u201d; p.146 labels the October special-dividend payment \\u201cSubsequent Event.\\u201d These disclosures may be tagged as subsequent events, not rolled into September 30 balances or FY2024 cash flows. The declaration/accrual versus payment distinction must survive downstream extraction.\\n\\n### Preparation record \\u2014 P1\\u2013P8\\n\\n| Responsibility | Execution and limitation |\\n|---|---|\\n| P1 Inventory / identity | Two pinned representations inventoried above; one content-verified issuer source. |\\n| P2 Triage | Read front matter and indexes; searched statement and MD&A headings; sampled beginning, middle and end. Annual statement content, not unrelated legal/market work, determined the route. |\\n| P3 Execution | Used page-addressed PDF text reads and searches. Runtime preparation is fresh pypdf layout extraction; no earlier preparation record exists. No OCR, visual render, external retrieval or ZIP operation was performed. |\\n| P4 Quality | Read all required primary statement text pp.105\\u2013109 and all notes pp.110\\u2013153. Checked period/unit headers and statement-to-index locators. Text-aid reads of pp.1 and 105\\u2013109 agree with the corresponding PDF-tool text in the examined passages; this is same-source representation comparison only. |\\n| P5 Active representation | Direct PDF-tool text is active for evidence; JSONL is an auxiliary aid. No new financial table or normalized dataset was created. |\\n| P6 Locators | Use one-based physical PDF pages in this handoff. Printed body p.99 is PDF p.101; printed F-3 is PDF p.105. Do not confuse printed and physical pagination. Ma