oceeds from both fourth quarter of fiscal 2024 issuances were used, along with existing cash on hand, to fund a $75.00 special dividend declaration\\u201d. | Debt-funded distributions retain debt service while transferring cash outside the creditor perimeter. \\u2192 Do not assume operating cash generation will be applied to deleveraging. Limitation: Policy is management language; documented issuance supports the behavioral interpretation. No target leverage or current policy update established. |\\n| GT02 Distributions / Shareholder extraction risk | September 2024 special dividend declaration was funded by new secured debt and cash; payment followed in October 2024. **Creditor-Adverse; High; Analyst Interpretation.** | S1 p.42 Significant Transactions, 2024-09-19: \\u201cTotal cash payments, funded by a combination of $3,000 million in new senior secured debt (as previously noted) and existing cash on hand, related to the special dividend and dividend equivalents were approximately $4,348 million. These payments were made in October 2024.\\u201d | Committed shareholder cash outflow reduces retained liquidity while incremental secured borrowing increases debt claims. \\u2192 Treat the year-end dividend payable as an earmarked cash call, not surplus liquidity. Limitation: October payment is a subsequent event, not FY2024 cash flow. Legal capacity untested. |\\n| GT03 Acquisition pattern / Acquisition appetite | Acquisition strategy targets proprietary aerospace components with aftermarket content; FY2024 acquisitions include CPI, Raptor, SEI, FPT and Extant product lines. **Mixed; High; Analyst Interpretation.** | S1 p.4 Business: \\u201cWe also maintain a selective acquisition strategy, concentrating on proprietary commercial aerospace component businesses with significant aftermarket content\\u201d; p.115 CPI, 2024-06-06: \\u201cThe acquisition was financed through existing cash on hand, inclusive of a portion of the cash proceeds from the new long-term debt issue