not establish debt funding of this distribution. | Behaviour type amendment covers refinancing here, not a claimed coercive amendment. No conclusion of priming or prohibited conduct. |\\n\\n#### T2D.5\\u2013T2D.8 \\u2014 ownership/support, allocation, disclosure and legal linkage\\n\\nO01\\u2013O06 and GT04/GT05/GT09 preserve unknown ownership stakes, governance safeguards and support. TX01\\u2013TX06 and H02\\u2013H15 capture repeated acquisitions, distributions, repurchases and refinancings without inferring appetite from one deal. GT08 captures genuine reporting evidence separately from missing proxy transparency. The S1 p.104 goodwill critical-audit-matter passage calls valuation \\u201ccomplex and judgmental\\u201d and sensitive to discount rates, revenue growth and EBITDA margins: this supports acquisition-valuation uncertainty, not a forecast impairment charge or failed audit.\\n\\n**Legal capacity \\u2260 willingness \\u2260 feasibility.** S1 p.16 lists covenants restricting debt, distributions, investments, liens, asset sales, affiliates and unrestricted subsidiaries, \\u201csubject, in each case, to certain important exceptions.\\u201d This does not quantify any basket. Actual distributions demonstrate willingness then; completed financing demonstrates historical feasibility then; neither proves present contractual permission, future market access or repeat payment capacity. Missing operative agreements prevent headroom, collateral-release, portability, dropdown, priming or restricted-payment calculations. Note-guarantee summaries on pp.127\\u2013132 are not recovery conclusions. No expected recovery or instrument recommendation is made.\\n\\n#### T2D.9 \\u2014 conflicts register (logged, not reconciled)\\n\\n| ID | Conflicting located spans, with every side retained | Disposition and impact |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| CF01 inherited U1 F3: maturity placement | S1 p.126 row: \\u201c5.50% senior subordinated notes due 2027\\u201d / gross \\u201c2,650\\u201d; p.13