D | Evidence chain | Mechanic \\u2192 credit implication | Counterevidence / named conflict |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| CT01 Revenue durability is installed-base, not contractual | B03\\u2013B04/B07: p.4 lifecycle/aftermarket estimates and historical stability claim; B09 p.13 lack of long-term aftermarket commitments. | Replacement needs can support repeat sales through a long aircraft life, but flight activity, customer finances and cancellable orders drive realization \\u2192 resilient opportunity set, not guaranteed debt-service receipts. | Commercial OEM and defense cycles remain; B04 has no channel margin statistic. |\\n| CT02 Margin/cash resilience is conditional | B08 supply certification/fixed-price costs; B11 U1 CF15/CF16, CF22/CF23; U1 EB05/NB01. | Mix and overhead absorption can help earnings, while working capital, interest, taxes and investment consume cash \\u2192 use GAAP cash and non-GAAP earnings separately, do not treat add-backs as spendable liquidity. | Management value-pricing language does not establish cost pass-through; purchase allocations/open controls add uncertainty. CF02 limits lease wording conclusions. |\\n| CT03 Customer diversification is incomplete protection | B02 multiple products; B05 customer/distributor concentration; B06 geography; B12 defense procurement/certification. | Individual product spread does not prevent correlated aerospace demand, purchasing bottlenecks or government actions \\u2192 monitor channel/customer inventory and regulatory dependencies. | Source's diversified-base characterization is management language, not adopted. CF04 prevents exact-threshold conclusions. |\\n| CT04 Operating growth need not deleverage | U1 CF22/CF24/CF28, KP09/KP15/KP16 and BS14; GT01/GT02, BF01/BF02; p.131 direct use-of-proceeds quote. | Cash generation coexists with acquisitions and distributions; new secured borrowing supports owner payout while year-end cash awaits settlement \\u2192 do not equate lower cash-net leverage with durable creditor cash retention. | November payout is cash funded, not automatically a recap; October cash settlement is subsequent. CF03 blocks a precise securitization flow reconstruction. |\\n| CT05 Mixed creditor history and no inferred support | GT06/BF03 par redemptions/extensions versus secured replacement; GT04 support missing. | Historical refinancing helps selected maturity runway but claim-priority change matters to creditor control; unidentified owner resources cannot be a backstop \\u2192 examine operative documents and stress independent debt service. | No coercive LME evidenced; no proof none ever occurred. CF01 blocks aggregate maturity-year conclusions, CF02 remains open. Missing support is not negative support behavior. |\\n| CT06 Committee readiness is bounded | GT08 audited reporting/scope exclusions; GT05/GT07/GT09 and U0/U1 gaps. | Annual evidence allows a historical business/funding debate; missing control/legal/update evidence prevents present underwriting and covenant conclusions \\u2192 escalate specific missing documents, not a blanket adverse governance assertion. | Supportive reporting evidence must survive extraction concerns; unresolved CF01\\u2013CF04 are explicit challenge items. |\\n\\n## Calculations\\n\\n### T2D.11 \\u2014 governance rubric calculation and retained exact results\\n\\nCalled **`score_governance`**, existing row checks and unchanged governance_sponsor_score, with GT01\\u2013GT09 and BF01\\u2013BF03 as documented above. Exact schema-compatible fields were used: topic behavior/funding/capacity fields null; flags all populated. Tool scoring is a calculation, **not evidence verification, not a certification and not a current issuer rating**. Reporting-quality supportive evidence was not used to score absent proxy disclosure transparency. Duplicate topic/action evidence is retained as input lineage, not manually weighted or averaged.\\n\\n| Tool-return dimension (exact) | score (exact string) | deciding input rows |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Leverage tolerance | `5` | GT01 |\\n| Shareholder extraction risk | `5` | GT02, BF01, BF02 |\\n| Acquisition appetite | `3` | GT03 |\\n| Support behavior | `Not Scorable` | [] |\\n| Disclosure transparency | `Not Scorable` | [] |\\n| Creditor treatment / amendment behavior | `3` | GT06, BF03 |\\n| Legal-capacity linkage | `Not Scorable` | [] |\\n| Reporting quality | `1` | GT08 |\\n| Related-party leakage risk | `Not Scorable` | [] |\\n\\nExact tool aggregate: **`composite: \\\"5\\\"`; `risk_level: \\\"High\\\"`; `high_risk_action: true`**. No manual score, invented weighting, missing-dimension zero or inferred sponsor score. High-risk-action evidence is the directly documented debt-funded special dividend declaration, distinct from unobserved sponsor support and distinct from mixed ordinary refinancing. Missing dimensions remain unscorable even though the tool supplies a composite. Tool `deciding` entries correspond to the actual facts, citations, mechanics and limitations in the input register, not additional evidence.\\n\\nNo new financial sum or ratio calculation was performed. U1 KP07/KP09/KP10/KP15/KP16 are retained existing outputs, not recomputed or restated. Their calculation lineage: consolidated USD millions; U1 C02 = CF22 plus signed CF23 (S1 p.109); C03 = BS17 + BS11 + BS12 (p.105), finance leases already included; C04 = D16 gross + D01 gross (pp.126\\u2013127); C10 = C03 / NB01; C11 = (C03 \\u2212 BS01) / NB01, annual non-GAAP denominator p.142. Values and periods are retained above; no covenant metric is implied. All additional source quantities are quoted/reported, not estimates created by this module.\\n\\n### Duty completion index\\n\\n| Responsibility | Delivered register / boundary |\\n|---|---|\\n| T2D.1 Identity, scope and ownership context | Sources; B01; O01\\u2013O06; exact U0/U1 hashes, reporting perimeter and dates |\\n| T2D.2 Dated history and source classification | H01\\u2013H20; B/TX/O rows; subsequent events segregated |\\n|