cial-dividend payment of 4,216 USD millions and dividend-equivalent payment of 132 USD millions**. These are reported subsequent events, not September 30 balances or FY2024 cash-flow entries. No post-payment cash balance, subsequent debt total or pro forma leverage is calculated here.\\n\\n## Gaps\\n\\nInherited readiness is **ready with limitations for the retrospective annual base**, not blocked for that bounded synthesis. CP-1A's Critical G01 and qualified CP-2 readiness are explicitly carried below; confidence remains Medium. Restrictions are not adverse issuer findings.\\n\\n| ID / severity | Inherited reference / missing or unresolved item | Why it matters / affected conclusion | Concrete action and gate |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| G01 \\u2014 Critical for current/live work | CP-1A G01; CP-0/CP-1 G3\\u2013G5: no current mandate/deal, interim/update, independent market/rating or portfolio pack; report postdates as-of | Prevents current underwriting, timely backtest, current-access and transaction-pro-forma claims | Obtain separately authorized dated mandate, interim and market inputs before expanding scope. Historical annual synthesis can proceed. |\\n| G02 \\u2014 High | CP-1A G02, O02/O04, GT04/GT05/GT09; CP-0/CP-1 G6: proxy, ultimate control, voting, safeguards, support and related-party evidence absent | Limits ownership, support and full governance assessment; no support uplift or adverse leakage inference | Obtain dated proxy, ownership/control and support/related agreements. Keep unsupported subtopics Not Assessable. |\\n| G03 \\u2014 High | CP-1A G03/GT07; CP-1 G4/F2: executed debt, security/intercreditor, guarantee/restricted-group documents, amendments and certificates absent | Prevents covenant headroom, RP/debt/lien/investment capacity, release permission and complete creditor-control conclusions | CP-4 to review operative documents and certificates; keep actual willingness separate from permission and future feasibility. |\\n| G04 \\u2014 High | CP-1 F3; CP-1A G04/CF01\\u2013CF04: maturity-year placement, lease wording, draw precision and customer-boundary conflicts retained | Blocks validated maturity ladder/aggregate refinancing wall and precise securitization flow bridge; limits concentration precision | Reconcile source-table fidelity and operative instrument terms. Do not choose an invented corrected schedule or double-count finance leases. |\\n| G05 \\u2014 Medium/high | CP-1 F1/F4; CP-1A G05: cash/noncash and recurrence detail for add-backs, normalized working capital, sustaining capex, price/volume and channel margins absent | Limits adjusted earnings, sustainable FCF, margin stress and cash conversion normalization | CP-1D challenge with cost detail; obtain channel/working-capital/capex evidence before cash-earnings or stress quantification. |\\n| G06 \\u2014 High for forward feasibility | CP-1 F2; CP-1A G06: cash access/restrictions, unconditional facility drawability, borrowing-base/LC conditions incomplete | Prevents usable liquidity-buffer/runway conclusion; headline net leverage lacks cash-use qualification | Build a dated liquidity bridge with accessible cash, declared payments, facility tests and actual service dates; no inferred shortfall. |\\n| G07 \\u2014 Medium | CP-1A G07/GT08: preliminary acquisition allocations, ICFR exclusions, no demonstrated acquired-unit returns/synergy bridge or future budget | Limits integration, valuation and acquisition-return confidence | Obtain final allocations, control-integration evidence and unit cash returns; do not assume strategy equals realized success. |\\n| G08 \\u2014 Medium | CP-0/CP-1 G1\\u2013G2; CP-1A G08: no visual/full-file fidelity assurance, text-only coverage boundaries | Limits cell-alignment and whole-report completeness claims | Obtain visual/source-table review for challenged material cells; preserve source/representation limitations in publication. |\\n| G09 \\u2014 Medium | CP-1A G09/H20/TX07: complete ownership, disposal, ratings/regulatory and prior-LME chronology unavailable | Prevents complete historical event or no-adverse-event assertions | Seek targeted dated evidence if needed. Absence in the bounded register is not proof of absence. |\\n| G10 \\u2014 Readiness/production restriction | CP-1A Next module: CP-2 ready with limitations; CP-1A G10 and CP-0/CP-1 G7: this is an intermediate handoff | Qualified upstream readiness caps confidence and does not establish a complete snapshot or delivered artifacts | Preserve all limitations; CP-OS must invoke separate report/HTML Model/charts/calculation-JSON delivery and verify populated outputs. No native accepted head or completed delivery is implied. |\\n\\n## Next module\\n\\n| Recipient / actual role | Concrete use of this synthesis | Required next evidence or restriction |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| CP-2A \\u2014 downside/stress | Quantify the operational \\u2192 revenue \\u2192 margin \\u2192 cash \\u2192 liquidity \\u2192 leverage/refinancing chain; test cost recovery, absorption and working-capital behavior | Obtain channel sensitivities, cost structure, sustaining capex and usable cash; no unsupported numerical thresholds. |\\n| CP-2D \\u2014 liquidity bridge/runway | Start with CP-1 reported cash, payable, operating-cash and facility observations; separately place October subsequent events | Resolve G06 and dated debt-service/cash-use timing; do not use the annual proxy as funding capacity. |\\n| CP-1D \\u2014 earnings-quality challenge | Test issuer add-back recurrence/cash character and reconcile ordinary EBITDA, EBITDA As Defined and CFO | Resolve G05; retain separate earnings bases and no automatic acceptance/rejection of adjustments. |\\n| CP-3C \\u2014 refinancing/liability-management risk | Use E5/E6, historical refinancing counterevidence and the qualified funding structure | Resolve maturity conflicts and obtain operative terms, consent history and dated access/liquidity evidence; no aggregate wall or future LME-permission conclusion yet